# p_4f8c — Hana Works from the Kitchen Table; Notebook Stays at the Desk

Hana's weekday morning is split between two surfaces. She eats breakfast at the kitchen table (07:30–09:00) with her tablet propped up beside her bowl, and she continues light work or reading from the kitchen table until about 10:00. After that she drifts to the living room and the tablet ends up on the coffee_table_l1 until roughly 12:00, when she puts it back on her nightstand. Her notebook, by contrast, never leaves desk_b1: it is her reference material for the afternoon-to-night shift, and she keeps it at the desk all day (confirmed: 4/4 sighted days, single receptacle desk_b1). Her mug follows her to the coffee table around 10:00 and stays there until she returns from work at 23:00.

Priya's routine is standard: morning walk 07:00–09:00 (weekday) or 10:00–12:00 (weekend), afternoon errands 14:00–16:00 (weekday). The guitar stays in Hana's bedroom. The camera stays on the bookshelf. The yoga mat stays in wardrobe_b2.

What sets this apart: tablet_hana is at kitchen_table_k1 from 08:00 to 10:00 on weekdays (not at desk_b1, not at nightstand_b1). The mug is at coffee_table_l1 from 10:00 to 17:00 on both days. The notebook is at desk_b1 all day. What would refute it: tablet_hana sighted at desk_b1 between 08:00 and 10:00 on a weekday; mug_hana sighted at desk_b1 or kitchen_table_k1 between 10:00 and 17:00.

